    "system": {
        "description": {
            "value": "<p>A shark's tooth in your hands, a swim Speed, and water whenever you want it.</p><p>You can <strong>breathe water</strong>, and you can create water freely from the gill-slits along the blade.</p><hr /><p><em>pf2e automates no drowning and has no \"breathes water\" field, so the nearest thing it does have is said instead: the <strong>amphibious</strong> creature trait, which its own glossary defines as breathing in water and in air. It shows on the sheet and a predicate can read it. Whether the water is there at all remains the GM's to say.</em></p>"
